---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
const unified = process.env.PIT_UNIFIED_PREVIEW === "1";
const hosted = process.env.PIT_HOSTED_STAGING === "1";
---
<Layout title="Guide" description="How to use PIT Crypto's free tools, blockchain inspections and operation previews safely.">
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">PIT</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Guide</span></nav>
  <header class="guide-intro">
    <p class="guide-overline">The PIT Crypto handbook</p>
    <h1>Start with the task.<br /><span>Know the boundary.</span></h1>
    <p>Use a calculator, inspect a chain or prepare an operation. This guide explains what each step does before you act.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="guide-start">
    <div class="guide-section-heading"><span>01</span><h2 id="guide-start">Choose your starting point</h2></div>
    <div class="guide-paths">
      <article><div><span class="guide-path-number">01</span><h3>Toolbox</h3><p>Run calculations and work with local data. No wallet, account or network request is needed in the isolated Toolbox build.</p></div>{unified && <a href="/toolbox/">Explore Toolbox</a>}</article>
      <article><div><span class="guide-path-number">02</span><h3>Explorer</h3><p>Inspect public chain data without signing. The public RPC provider can see the addresses you query; results are snapshots, not a full ownership inventory.</p></div>{unified && <a href="/explorer/">Explore Explorer</a>}</article>
      <article><div><span class="guide-path-number">03</span><h3>Operations</h3><p>Configure, review and simulate a transaction before signing. Execution is currently limited to local Anvil chain 31337. {hosted && "This hosted preview cannot connect or send."}</p></div><a href="/#directory">Browse operations</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section guide-essentials" aria-labelledby="guide-before">
    <div class="guide-section-heading"><span>02</span><h2 id="guide-before">Before you sign</h2></div>
    <div class="guide-essentials-grid">
      <article><h3>Price and network cost</h3><p>Most tools are free. Proposed USDC service fees are inactive outside the local MOCK-USDC demonstration. Network gas is separate and paid in native ETH. PIT does not combine them into a made-up total.</p><p>In the local atomic payment path, a reverted operation does not retain the service fee. Its gas, and gas for a separate approval, can still be spent. A confirmed creation or distribution is generally irreversible.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Permissions and custody</h3><p>Never provide a seed phrase or private key. Token creation roles go to the creator, not PIT. Review each ERC-20 spender and amount; revoke excess allowances when appropriate.</p><p>ERC-721 per-token approval differs from ERC-1155 collection-wide operator approval. Lockers and vesting contracts hold tokens on-chain until their release rules permit a claim. Review the beneficiary, funding and schedule before signing.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section guide-footnotes" aria-labelledby="guide-data">
    <div class="guide-section-heading"><span>03</span><h2 id="guide-data">Data and availability</h2></div>
    <div class="guide-footnotes-grid">
      <div><h3>What leaves your browser?</h3><p>Free calculations and locally prepared CSV or metadata stay client-side where feasible. Public RPC queries disclose queried addresses to that provider. On-chain transactions publish addresses and amounts. The metadata studio prepares files; PIT does not host or pin them to IPFS.</p></div>
      <div><h3>What is still a preview?</h3><p>Public paid checkout, mainnet execution, merchant payouts and live premium-report sales are unavailable. The x402 experiment uses simulated verification and settlement. Browser-extension acceptance, an independent contract audit and commercial and legal reviews remain ahead.</p><p>Permissionless contracts may also be called directly outside PIT’s guided workflow.</p></div>
    </div>
    {unified && <p class="guide-links"><a href="/toolbox/privacy/">Toolbox privacy</a><a href="/toolbox/legal/">Site information</a></p>}
  </section>
</Layout>
